From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] aic8800_fdrv: bound the association IE lengths to their
 buffer

rwnx_rx_sm_connect_ind() passes assoc_req_ie_len and assoc_rsp_ie_len
from the device to cfg80211_find_ie(), cfg80211_connect_result() and
cfg80211_roamed(). The IEs live in the fixed assoc_ie_buf[]
(SM_ASSOC_IE_LEN bytes) and the lengths are not checked against it, so a
large value reads past the buffer.

If both lengths together exceed the buffer, set them to 0 and count the
case in rx_bad_frame_drops. The connect result is still reported, so the
connection state does not hang.

Assisted-by: Claude

diff --git a/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_msg_rx.c b/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_msg_rx.c
index dd7ff5e..95ff58a 100644
--- a/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_msg_rx.c
+++ b/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_msg_rx.c
@@ -980,6 +980,15 @@ static inline int rwnx_rx_sm_connect_ind(struct rwnx_hw *rwnx_hw,
 	dev = rwnx_vif->ndev;
     wdev = dev->ieee80211_ptr;
 
+    /* Both IE lengths come from the device and must fit in assoc_ie_buf.
+     * Otherwise the IEs are dropped and the result is still reported. */
+    if ((u32)ind->assoc_req_ie_len + ind->assoc_rsp_ie_len >
+        sizeof(ind->assoc_ie_buf)) {
+        rx_bad_frame_drops++;
+        ind->assoc_req_ie_len = 0;
+        ind->assoc_rsp_ie_len = 0;
+    }
+
     /* Retrieve IE addresses and lengths */
     req_ie = (const u8 *)ind->assoc_ie_buf;
     rsp_ie = req_ie + ind->assoc_req_ie_len;
